# November 21, 2026: northern Greene County, the hill country just south of the Albany County line: Oak Hill,
# Durham, East Durham and Cornwallville (Town of Durham), Greenville and Norton Hill (Town of Greenville), and the
# Bronck farm at Coxsackie. Drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny (region albco), which offered Greenville
# and Oak Hill; the Atlas had nothing in either. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text
# (tools/wiki_raw.py), the National Register forms for Christ Church (2015), the Oak Hill Historic District (2017) and
# the Cornwallville Cemetery (2017) through NPGallery's text layer, HMdb markers, the Episcopal Diocese of Albany's
# page for Christ Church, the Greene County Historical Society's tour page, Upstater, and the Greene County Historical
# Journal (vol. 7 no. 4) for the Prevost manor house, all through tools/page.py.
from data_b import N
